# Chapter 10 (Normal Subgroups and Factor Groups) — pain points & missing machinery

A log kept WHILE transliterating Chapter 10, recording what the 2b4m language or standard
library lacked at the moment it blocked a proof. Entries that are ADDRESSED get removed
rather than annotated. Plain markdown without a `.md` extension so the literate checker
never parses it.

Same discipline as CHAPTER5/6/7/9-PAINPOINTS: a claim here is a claim about the CHECKER AS
IT IS, re-probed, not a recollection. And per Chapter 9's lesson — **a claim of "cannot be
done" requires a FAILED PROBE, not a search of std.**

